    <h1>Scientific Core Library Stack {{ release_version }}</h1>
    <table class="invisible-table" style="border: none;">
        <tr>
            <td class="left" style="border: none;">
                <img src="logo.gif" alt="SCLS Logo" style="width: 100%;">
            </td>
            <td class="right" style="border: none;">
                <p>SCLS is a curated build and packaging system for scientific computing libraries. It produces a consistent, tested stack of numerical libraries that work together: BLAS/LAPACK, sparse solvers, graph partitioners, MPI, I/O libraries, and their dependencies.</p>

                <p>The stack is available as RPM packages for Enterprise Linux (Rocky, Alma, RHEL) and as direct prefix installs for macOS and other Unix systems. All installations are kept in <code>/opt/scls/&lt;flavor&gt;</code> to not interfere with the operating system.</p>

                <p>Send comments, questions or suggestions to <b id="email">Christian Messe: [javascript protected email]</b></p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Design Philosophy</h3>
    <p>SCLS is deliberately opinionated. It makes choices so the resulting stack remains coherent:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>GCC is the default toolchain for its open availability and strong Fortran support.</li>
        <li>OpenMPI is the default MPI implementation.</li>
        <li>Shared libraries are the normal target.</li>
        <li>LP64 (32-bit integers) is the default; ILP64 is supported where needed.</li>
        <li>Numerical correctness matters more than aggressive optimization &mdash; no <code>-ffast-math</code>.</li>
        <li>Packages are BSD-3 compatible where possible; GPL-3 packages are flagged and not distributed.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Flavors</h3>
    <p>A <em>flavor</em> defines the compiler, math backend, and optimization choices for the entire stack. Each flavor is a self-contained installation.</p>
    <ul>
        {% for group in flavor_groups %}
        <li><strong>{{ group.title }}</strong>
            <p>{{ group.description }}</p>
            <ul>
                {% for flavor in group.flavors %}
                <li><code><b>{{ flavor.name }}</b></code> &mdash; {{ flavor.description }}</li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
            <br>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>

    <h3>Installation on Enterprise Linux 9</h3>
    <p>To install a flavor, download the release package and run:</p>
    <code><b>sudo dnf install <a href="https://belfem.lbl.gov/scls/el9/x86_64/scls-release-{{ release_version }}-1.el9.noarch.rpm">scls-release-{{ release_version }}-1.el9.noarch.rpm</a></b></code><br>
    <code><b>sudo dnf install scls-&lt;flavor&gt;</b></code><br>
    <p>After installation, activate the environment:</p>
    <code><b>source /opt/scls/&lt;flavor&gt;/bin/activate</b></code><br>
    <p>This adds the stack's <code>bin/</code> and <code>lib/</code> to your paths and sets the <code>SCLS</code> environment variable.</p>

    <h3>macOS</h3>
    <p>On macOS (Intel and Apple Silicon), SCLS builds from source using the Unix builder. The <code>macos</code> flavor builds its own GCC for Fortran support and installs to a local prefix. See the <a href="https://github.com/cmesse/scls">Git repository</a> for instructions.</p>

    <h3>Integer Indexing</h3>
    <p>All libraries are compiled with 32-bit integer indexing (LP64) by default. ILP64 (64-bit) builds can be produced from the same recipes by selecting the appropriate flavor configuration.</p>

    <h3>Git Repository</h3>
    <p>To build your own flavor or contribute recipes:<br><br>
    <code><b><a href="https://github.com/cmesse/scls">git clone https://github.com/cmesse/scls.git</a></b></code></p>

    <h3>Packages</h3>
    <table class="package-table">
        <tr class="gray-bg">
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Version</th>
            <th>License</th>
            <th>Description</th>
            {% for flavor in flavors %}
            <th class="flavor-header">{{ flavor.name }}</th>
            {% endfor %}
        </tr>
        {% for package in packages %}
        <tr {% if loop.index is odd %}class="gray-bg"{% endif %}>
            <td class="left">
                {% if package.homepage %}
                <a href="{{ package.homepage }}" class="package-name">{{ package.name }}</a>
                {% else %}
                <span class="package-name">{{ package.name }}</span>
                {% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="center">{{ package.version }}</td>
            <td class="left">{{ package.license }}</td>
            <td class="left">{{ package.summary }}</td>
            {% for flavor in flavors %}
            <td class="center-check">
                {% if package|package_available(flavor.name) %}
                &#10003;
                {% else %}
                -
                {% endif %}
            </td>
            {% endfor %}
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
    </table>
    <br>

    <h3>Known Issues</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><b>STRUMPACK</b> &mdash; Tests <code>SPARSE_HODLR_mpi_1</code> and <code>SPARSE_mpi_16</code> fail on systems with fewer than 10 CPU cores due to MPI oversubscription.</li>
        <li><b>SuperLU_DIST</b> &mdash; MPI tests disabled; they require more cores than typically available on build VMs.</li>
        <li><b>Slate</b> &mdash; The <code>heev</code> tests fail.</li>
    </ul>

